cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the real-data benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "City Health Index Audit (CHIA): an open-source measurement audit toolkit and dashboard"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "City Health Index Audit (CHIA) contributors"
    website: "https://github.com/<OWNER>/city-health-audit"
version: 0.6.0
date-released: "2026-11-10"
repository-code: "https://github.com/<OWNER>/city-health-audit"
url: "https://<OWNER>.github.io/city-health-audit/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An open-source measurement-audit toolkit and static dashboard for evaluating
  in-use city health indices. The project does not publish city rankings. All
  shipped values are computed from real public data: the China City
  Statistical Yearbook prefecture-level panel (302 cities, 2003-2018) and the
  WHO Ambient Air Quality Database V6.1 as an independent cross-source
  validation. The toolkit reports cross-source consistency, per-indicator
  coverage and lineage, Monte Carlo grade stability under random weighting,
  and first-order variance decomposition of construction choices.
keywords:
  - urban health
  - healthy cities
  - composite indicators
  - measurement audit
  - cross-source validation
  - reproducible research
  - health equity
notes: >-
  Replace <OWNER> with the GitHub account or organisation before the first
  release. Papers should additionally cite the underlying data sources
  (see data/raw/SOURCE.md), the OSF preregistration and the Zenodo archive
  DOI once minted; see docs/PAPER_PLAN.md.
